# Steward — Status (AGENT 1)

**Last updated:** 2026-01-01 — scaffolded; not yet written by its agent.

> **This file answers exactly one question: what is TRUE NOW.** It is *overwritten*, never prepended
> — the previous answer is not history worth keeping, it is a **wrong answer**; git holds the
> history. Budget ~200 lines (`/crit-doc-lint [8]` warns past it, or on a second dated "as of" section).
> Full contract: `.critos/system/contract-memory.md § 1`.

## Now true

`<The current state of this domain, in the present tense. What is live, what the real numbers are,
what is deployed, what is broken. No dates-as-narrative: a fact that needs a date carries it inline
(2026-01-01), but this section is not a timeline.>`

## Next (my domain)

`<Vertical micro-steps that are mine alone — COMMITTED work only: if nobody says yes, it still has
to happen. A parked item lives here WITH its un-park trigger. Shared/cross-domain efforts do NOT
live here — they are ROADMAP rows.>`

### ⛔ This file does not list what is OPEN across agents. Ask the inbox.

```
bash ~/.claude/skills/crit-status-check/status-check.sh --me 1 .critos/memory/a1 --domain <code-path>
```

Cross-agent obligations live in `HANDOFFS.md`, which **outranks this snapshot**. A file that may not
*assert* what is open cannot assert it *stalely* — that is the rule at enforcement tier 1, and it is
why "what do I owe?" is a **query, not a recall**.

